        <history>
          <p>Subtitled ‘Sinfonia espansiva’, the Third Symphony reflects an expansive, life-affirming mood that Nielsen contrasted with the darker tone of his later Fourth. Its second movement features two wordless solo voices, an unusual and much-noted touch for a symphonic slow movement of its era.</p>
